}{
  "_comment": [
    "Battle scene settings (Battle System v2: the Attack and Defense bars move on their own; tap one to act).",
    "Each bar starts slow and speeds up to its top speed on a curve (the equipped gear sets both; with none:",
    "starts at 15, top speed 200, reached after 1.8 s, on a bar 120 long). The two are scaled separately:",
    "bar_slow_speed_scale: multiplies the slow start (1 = as the gear sets it; lower = even slower start).",
    "bar_fast_speed_scale: multiplies the top speed it speeds up to (higher = faster after the slow start).",
    "bar_cooldown_ms: after a tap, how long that bar waits (milliseconds) before it moves again.",
    "Read when the game starts; without this file the game uses 1, 1 and 1500.",
    "attack_pause_ms: while the player or the enemy attacks, BOTH sides' clocks pause this long (the bars do not",
    "move or cool down, the enemy's clock waits) -- the owner's rule, docs/30_GAMEPLAY_PLAN.md Â§4. 0 turns it off.",
    "hit_number_delay_ms: the damage number appears this long after the attack starts (when the swing lands)."
  ],
  "bar_slow_speed_scale": 0.5,
  "bar_fast_speed_scale": 10,
  "bar_cooldown_ms": 1000,
  "attack_pause_ms": 450,
  "hit_number_delay_ms": 180
}
{
  "_comment": [
    "Per-character nudges for character clips (docs/15_ANIMATION.md, 'Characters'; e.g. media/anim/archer_bow.anim).",
    "A character clip is made with one character and fitted to any other automatically: its 'hand' (where the bow is",
    "held) keeps its share of the visible body's height and its distance from the body's right edge, measured from the",
    "sprite's pixels. A character whose hand still looks off gets an entry here: the sprite name and the hand's extra",
    "move in pixels, x right and y down. Example: \"player_viking\": { \"hand\": [0, -1] } lifts the bow one pixel.",
    "A character not listed needs nothing."
  ]
}
